{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Who sit.</b> To consult the dead and matters of demons." "<b>And in the niches.</b> Ruins, like \"a besieged city\" (Isaiah 1:8)." "<b>Those who eat the flesh of pigs.</b> To provoke me." "<b>And broth.</b> Known, as in \"pour out the broth\" (Judges 6:20). And it is written ופרק, and they are two names for one thing."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:59.694004596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}